| Function | What it swallows | Consequence |
|---|---|---|
| `upload()` | All exceptions from `http_post`; conflates transport error with non-OK response | Caller can't diagnose or retry; can't tell failure cause |
| `backup()` | `ofstream` open failure + write failure; returns `void` | Backup can silently do nothing while caller believes it succeeded |

The core theme: both functions convert "something went wrong" into a silent, undifferentiated success-looking result. `upload` at least returns a bool, but `backup` returns nothing at all — the worst case, since a failed backup is exactly the failure you'd most want to know about.

